## Model card

- **Name:** Space Bunny Alpha (also written `space-bunny-alpha`); free preview tier on OpenCode Zen is listed as **Space Bunny Free** (`opencode/space-bunny-free`).
- **Short description:** anonymous reasoning model from an unnamed provider, listed on OpenRouter under the `stealth` provider on 2026-09-23; 1M-token context, native image/video input, adjustable reasoning effort, and free during the preview window. The developer has not been disclosed — nothing in the listing identifies a lab.
- **Provider / access:** OpenRouter `stealth/space-bunny-alpha` (OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions, supports `reasoning`, `reasoning_effort`, `include_reasoning`, `tools`, `tool_choice`, `response_format`, streaming); OpenCode Zen `opencode/space-bunny-free`. OpenRouter states it is only the routing layer, not the developer.
- **Release / knowledge:** listing live 2026-09-23 (OpenRouter); knowledge cutoff not disclosed.
- **IDs:** `stealth/space-bunny-alpha` (OpenRouter) and `space-bunny-free` (OpenCode Zen, per this folder's `meta.json`).
- **Context window:** 1,000,000 tokens with `top_provider.max_completion_tokens` 524,288 (OpenRouter endpoint API, checked 2026-09-23/24) — provider-listed capacity, not a measured retrieval result.
- **Modalities:** text, image and video in; text out; reasoning mandatory (efforts low → max, medium default); tool calling and JSON mode; OpenRouter telemetry rows also list web search and image output as capability flags (unverified).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-09-25):** $0 per 1M input and output during the preview (OpenRouter); Zen free tier described as limited-time. Post-preview pricing not disclosed. Stealth terms allow the anonymous provider to retain prompts/completions (not used for training) — do not send private code or customer data.
- **Architecture:** undisclosed. Identity hypotheses in circulation (unverified): MiniMax family (24/24 tokenizer probe deltas matched named MiniMax endpoints per one independent probe set) and an OpenAI GPT-OSS-style model (a reconstructed prompt resembles the Harmony format). Neither is confirmed; the name carries no vendor signal (this stealth series has previously been GLM, MiMo, LongCat and Unpareto models).

### Raw benchmarks found

> Nothing below produced a verified public benchmark score for this exact model
> ID as of 2026-09-25. Every model-quality row reads "no verified public score
> found"; the measured numbers that do exist are serving telemetry, not accuracy
> benchmarks, and are recorded separately below for traceability.

Agent / tool use: no verified public score found (no Terminal-Bench, Tau3-Banking, Tau2-Bench, GDPval-AA, SWE Atlas or Claw-Eval run has been published under this ID).

Reasoning / knowledge: no verified public score found (no GPQA Diamond, HLE, LCR/MLCR, CritPt or Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index result published; Artificial Analysis and Command Code both list the model as *not yet scored*).

Coding: no verified public score found (no SWE-bench Verified/Pro, LiveCodeBench, SciCode, Vibe Code Bench or DeepSWE run published; one tracker's "4 benchmarks" panel renders chart-only values that are not attributable to a named harness, and LM Market Cap's ranking composite is a signal-weighted score, not a benchmark result).

Long context: no long-context retrieval measurement found (the 1M window and 524,288-token output ceiling are provider listings only).

Measured serving telemetry (not benchmark scores):

- OpenRouter P50 throughput **79 tok/s** and P50 latency **0.93 s** (TPS, best provider, 2026-09-23); an independent field guide recorded **87 tok/s** and **1.07 s** (24 Sep snapshot, all efforts/locations)
- Availability: **76.22%** over the trailing 3 days counting errors/empty responses; **100%** when requests were routed to a provider (TPS, 2026-09-23) vs **94.98%** inference availability / 97.70% reachability (independent field guide, 24 Sep)
- Tokenizer probes: **24/24** token-count deltas matched named MiniMax endpoints (independent probe set, 24 Sep) — an identity clue, not a quality metric

